'''Harb Binli'''<ref name="UVG" /> was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Rebel pilot|pilot]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> from [[Eriadu]]<ref name="UVG" /> who served in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> During the war, [[Cadet]] Binli served as [[Red Seven]].<ref name="UVG" /><ref name="Geektionary" />

After returning from the [[Mission to Eadu]], [[Jyn Erso]] brought information about the threat of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] before the [[Alliance Cabinet]], as well as a gathering of various military personnel, including Binli, who was standing close to Erso and [[Bodhi Rook]]. Listening closely to the heated debate, the pilot acquiesced to Erso's plea for action. Soon after, he fought in the [[Battle of Scarif]], during which his [[Wingmate|wingman]] and friend [[Pedrin Gaul]] was [[Death|killed]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> He later served in the [[Battle of Yavin]], in which he was killed in action.<ref name="Duty" />

At some point prior to [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|RO}}</ref> Binli was scheduled Shift Cycle 2 of an [[T-65B X-wing starfighter|X-wing]] flight patrol mission along with fellow pilots Cdt. Pedrin Gaul ([[Red Five]]) and [[Lieutenant|Lt.]] [[Nozzo Naytaan]] ([[Red Nine]]). Their mission was to route from [[Yavin Prime|Yavin]] to [[Gordian Reach|Gordian]] Trace Relays, perform a flyby of surrounding space, then after verifying visual and sensor all clear, perform close uplink of passive relay recordings.<ref name="RebelFiles">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Binli_helmet.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Harb Binli's [[K-22995 light flight helmet|flight helmet]]]]
While a relatively recent addition to [[Red Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Red Squadron]], Binli's talent and tenacity meant he particularly excelled at strafing runs against point defense [[cannon]]s. He learned many lessons from his more experienced [[wingmate]] and teacher<ref name="Geektionary" /> [[Pedrin Gaul]].<ref name="UVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Harb Binli was portrayed by [[Benjamin Hartley]] in the 2016 film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="FotF">{{WebCite|url=https://thefutureoftheforce.com/2017/03/08/star-wars-a-pilots-perspective-benjamin-hartley-interview|text=Benjamin Hartley &#124; A Pilot's Perspective (Interview)|author=Roberts, Phil|date=2017-03-08|work=[https://thefutureoftheforce.com Future of the Force]|archivedate=20201202101311}}</ref>

